\ S6d probe A — DQ4 fence baseline, shared target (S6d-7.1). `next`'s row is
\ the S8-shaped App-headed protocol row; the impl target grounds as a bare
\ `Concrete(Type::Slice(..))`, so the S2-6 concrete-target fence fires at
\ desugar on the clean tree (`member_app_concrete_target_error`). The S6d-8
\ sentinel patch admits this exact spelling; on that tree the file builds and
\ the main below runs — one mono `next` step over a 5-element view prints the
\ element 3 and the remainder's length 4.
\
\ Body note (S6d-8.2): the prescribed Done arm (`drop Done`) is REJECTED by
\ the branch-join borrow rule — the More arm's Step carries the remainder
\ view's deriv, the Done arm's carries none, and the join refuses the
\ asymmetry. `as-done` (a poly word whose call-site output push, REQ-4d site
\ 4, forwards the dropped view's deriv onto the Step slot) gives both arms'
\ Step slots the same suspension, which is what lets the protocol shape
\ check at all. See the round report — this is a load-bearing workaround.
import: intrinsics * ;
import: core::prelude * ;
import: hosted::show | . | ;

type: Step['T 'Rest]
| Done
| More 'T 'Rest
;

trait: Iterator['It: * -> *]
: next inline ( 'It['T] -- Step['T 'It['T]] ) ;
;

\ Poly on purpose: a mono non-inline twin is banned at the word entry
\ (Ruling B), and an inline twin splices to `drop Done`, whose push carries
\ no deriv — the join disagreement again. The poly output slot is a declared
\ `Var`, which the signature audit treats as reference-free (the deferred
\ per-instantiation audit is the gap site 4's forward closes).
: as-done ['R] ( 'R -- Step[i64 'R] ) drop Done ;

impl: Iterator for Slice[i64]
: next
| s |
s dup len |n|
n 0 >usize eq
~[ as-done ]
~[
dup 0 >usize &> @ |v|
1 >usize n 1 >usize sub subslice
v swap More
]
if
;
;

: main ( -- )
3 5 fill |buf|
&buf slice
next
~[ ( Done ) drop ]
~[ ( More ) More> |v r| v . r len >i64 . ]
Step?
buf drop
;
